<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernest Louis, Grand Duke of Hesse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ernst Ludwig of Hesse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernest Louis, Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, reigned from 1892 to 1918 and was the last ruler of the Grand Duchy of Hesse. A grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandra-feodorovna-alix-of-hesse">Empress Alexandra of Russia</a>, he was a keen patron of the arts and in 1899 founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt-artists-colony">Darmstadt Artists' Colony</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mathildenhohe">Mathildenhöhe</a>, a centre of Jugendstil. He was deposed in the revolution of November 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernest-louis-grand-duke-of-hesse.jpg" alt="Ernest Louis, Grand Duke of Hesse" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernest_Louis_I_of_Hesse_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The last grand dukes, Louis IV and <b>Ernest Louis</b>, were constitutional monarchs who left much of the business of government to their ministers.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Grand Duchy of Hesse · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Grand Duke Ernest Louis</b> was deposed in November 1918, and Hesse-Darmstadt became the People's State of Hesse, with a democratic constitution adopted in December 1919.</blockquote><a href="/state/peoples-state-of-hesse">People's State of Hesse</a></li></ul></section>
